Third-party components (fetched or installed separately, not part of this repository):
- Express (MIT), ical.js (MPL-2.0), @simplewebauthn/server (MIT), qrcode (MIT), express-rate-limit (MIT): npm dependencies.
- sharp (Apache-2.0, Lovell Fuller), with libvips (LGPL-3.0-or-later) in its prebuilt npm packages
  (@img/sharp-*): draws pictures from elsewhere again before the board keeps them (server/images.ts).
- Fluent Emoji (MIT, Microsoft), https://github.com/microsoft/fluentui-emoji: the Clipart pictures,
  installed with the board from npm (@iconify-json/fluent-emoji-flat).
- More clipart styles, installed with the board from npm (@iconify-json/...) and unpacked into its
  data folder: Streamline Emojis (CC BY 4.0, Streamline, https://streamlinehq.com),
  Noto Emoji (Apache-2.0, Google), OpenMoji (CC BY-SA 4.0, https://openmoji.org), Twemoji
  (CC BY 4.0, Twitter), Firefox OS Emoji (Apache-2.0, Mozilla), EmojiOne 2 (CC BY 4.0, Emoji One) and
  IconPark (Apache-2.0, ByteDance), Meteocons (MIT, Bas Milius, https://meteocons.com) and Iconito
  (MIT, https://iconito.com). Shown in Pictures as they come, except that OpenMoji's and IconPark's
  black outlines are drawn in chalk white so they show on a dark board.
- Emojibase (MIT, Miles Johnson), https://emojibase.dev: the words that go with each emoji, so a
  search finds them (clipart/words.json, made by clipart/words.py from emojibase-data).
- Game Icons (CC BY 3.0), https://game-icons.net: the ✏️ chalk drawings (the family-friendly part of the set),
  installed with the board from npm (@iconify-json/game-icons). By Lorc, Delapouite and contributors.
- Noto Animated Emoji (CC BY 4.0, Google), https://googlefonts.github.io/noto-emoji-animation/:
  fetched on first use and cached locally.
- Google Fonts (SIL Open Font License): Dancing Script, Cormorant Garamond, Kalam, Caveat,
  Permanent Marker, Pacifico, Fredericka the Great, Amatic SC, Rock Salt, and the 55 others listed in
  shared/fonts.ts (Patrick Hand to Roboto); and Noto Color Emoji (Google),
  used only where a screen has no emoji of its own. Installed from npm (@fontsource; the emoji in the COLRv1
  format from @infolektuell/noto-color-emoji).
- Openclipart (public domain, CC0), https://openclipart.org: the best of its older collection as
  shipped by Debian (openclipart-svg), cleaned and cropped (clipart/openclipart.json.gz, made by
  clipart/openclipart.py).
- Openverse (WordPress.org), https://openverse.org: Pictures' "Look on the web" searches it for
  public-domain illustrations (CC0 or Public Domain Mark only), without an account; each picture's
  source is in its Openverse record.
- The "Garland & trims" pictures (clipart/garland.json, drawn by clipart/garland.py): drawn for this
  project and given to the public domain (CC0).
- React (MIT, Meta Platforms) for the screens, built with Vite (MIT).
- OpenCV (Apache-2.0) and the YuNet face detection model from opencv_zoo (MIT):
  optional face finder, installed by deploy/setup-face.sh.
- Weather data: Open-Meteo (CC BY 4.0), https://open-meteo.com/.
